(d/'README.md').write_text('''# Read-only cold-field forward/reverse ownership

Accepted progress remains **90%**, P7 open. No timing benchmark, full unit suite, commit or push.

The existing directory auditor now validates actual Entity Map/no competing ordinary ROW and no legacy selector for every group owner, direct hot references/presence, distinct cold reference masks, canonical row directories and all values, disjoint hot/cold fields, actual LargeValue contents and cross-block field totals. Blocks are decoded one at a time, not once per owner. Cold source adds no per-field directory entries. Reverse physical checks reject duplicate/orphan cold slots and membership records using exact logical slot generations and group-owned locators. RAW Edge covers cold owner-kind@7 rather than codec@6. Cold-only groups remain valid. Actual reference callbacks deliver once per reference row and never replay consumer failures.

Both experimental membership configurations pass **293 related module checks**, default **68**. Eleven new ownership checks cover positive/negative, actual LargeValues, wrong masks/global counts, orphan cold/membership records, malformed values behind valid outer checksums, local future-reference rejection, budgets/cancellation/refunds and read-only behavior. These use real pages/indexes/Entity Map with the existing private candidate descriptor, not public conversion acceptance. Initial failed reports are retained. The missing-account fixture was fixed; the generation fixture now explicitly forges its fault instead of assuming immutable logical generations equal metadata epochs. The error-code assertion became stricter, distinguishing local INVALID_HEADER from later manifest INVALID_STATE. No semantic guard was weakened.

**Normal new-mode production publication remains closed.** Mutation guards remain. Public conversion, full graph lifecycle and whole-database acceptance still need implementation. In particular, cold-owner LargeValue reachability/retirement cannot use the old explicit-selector iterator; partial/non-exhausted scans never authorize a sweep. Conversion, batching, mutation/demotion/delete/inverse, old pins/reopen/faults/retirement, mature whole allocation/migration bootstrap and the final matrix remain pending.
''')
